afk: distribution default settings via $OMP_DISTRO_CONFIG.

Motivation: the afk wrapper used to symlink the generated distribution
config.yml into the profile's agent dir. That made the *user's* global
config a read-only Nix-store symlink, so nothing the user changed at
runtime (model selection, setup wizard state, any /settings write)
survived a restart — omp writes runtime settings to the global
config.yml, and the wrapper clobbered it back on every launch.

This patch adds a distribution-defaults settings layer: when
$OMP_DISTRO_CONFIG names a YAML settings file, it is loaded into a
#distro layer merged BELOW the user's global config (and above the
schema defaults). Precedence becomes:

  schema defaults < distro defaults < global < project < overlays < runtime

so the distribution ships opinionated defaults while every user-level
write persists normally and overrides them. Loading is lenient: a
missing or malformed distro file degrades to {} with a logged warning
instead of bricking the binary.

What must survive a rebase:
- #distro merged as the LOWEST config layer of every merge (user config
  must always win): #rebuildMerged before 18.6.0, #mergeOwnLayers since
  (which also feeds pin settling and reload validation).
- Both #load() and #loadReadOnly() populate #distro; cloneForCwd copies
  it for root instances (reloadFromDisk/reloadForCwd re-read only the
  user layers and re-merge, so they need no change; overlays inherit it
  through their parent's merged view).
- List membership writes (writeMember) seed from the distro list when
  the global layer has none.
- The distro file goes through #loadYamlIfPresent and therefore
  #migrateRawSettings, same as the global config. #loadYamlIfPresent
  returns a TAGGED YamlLoadResult (since 17.2.1), not RawSettings:
  unwrap `kind === "loaded"` explicitly. Treating the result as a plain
  object merges `{kind, settings}` as junk keys and the whole layer
  silently vanishes — which takes skills.customDirectories, and with it
  the entire Superpowers library, down with it (tests/distro-config.test.ts).

Rebased 18.2.10 -> 18.6.0: upstream split Settings into overlay-aware
own layers (OwnLayers {global, project, configOverlay, overrides}) merged
by #mergeOwnLayers, which now backs #rebuildMerged AND soft-pin settling,
reloadFromDisk/reloadForCwd candidate validation. The distro layer is
therefore applied inside #mergeOwnLayers (lowest, before global) instead
of in #rebuildMerged, so every merge path sees it; it stays an instance
field rather than an OwnLayers member because no reload path re-reads
it. Overlay children keep #distro = {} (their parent's merged view
already carries it); cloneForCwd copies it in the root branch only.
New in 18.6.0: writeMember (Setting.setMember, e.g. task.disabledAgents
toggles) seeds from the global list or else the schema default; it now
falls back to the distro list first, so toggling one item never drops
the distribution's entries.

Rebased 18.12.6 -> 18.18.0: upstream runs subagents on worker threads
(task.workerThreads) whose Settings are mirrors of the main instance
(Settings.mirror / mirrorState / applyMirrorState) and never run init(),
so they would silently lose the distro layer. SettingsMirrorState now
carries `distro` and applyMirrorState adopts it; this must survive
rebases too. Ships test/config/distro-mirror.test.ts. The #mergeOwnLayers
line is wrapped to pass oxfmt.

